    "narrative": "**Taylor Ward** (71.19) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) headline today\u2019s roster as our elite offensive engines, primarily driven by a massive park factor boost and a targetable matchup against Avila (4.91 xERA). **Taylor Ward** benefits from an ideal third-spot placement in the order, while **Dylan Beavers** earns a strong grade despite a slight drag on his score due to the defensive profile of the opposing battery; both are locked in for high-ceiling production. **Bryce Harper** (69.66) remains a set-and-forget play in the heart of the order, with his elite xwOBA (0.399) providing a stable floor even against a quality arm like Flaherty.\n\nThe decision to bench **Daulton Varsho** (51.77) was the most difficult call of the morning. While **Daulton Varsho** offers the elite stolen base upside we prioritize, his efficiency score was dragged down by an unfavorable platoon split against Sears, causing him to fall behind the consistent production profiles of **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Luis Arraez**. Elsewhere, **Tyler Freeman** (62.67) and **Lawrence Butler** (63.24) represent high-efficiency starts; **Lawrence Butler** is particularly well-positioned at the top of the lineup to capitalize on a favorable platoon edge against Burke. We are monitoring **Masyn Winn** closely, as his sub-40 floor score against the dangerous Sale forced him to the bench, reinforcing our commitment to avoiding low-ceiling matchups that exhaust our limited daily game caps.",
